    },
    {
      "id": "ni7qaOtWzSbaa1hTEdaVA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 523.2554771703288,
      "y": 2924.7232080574304,
      "width": 1010.399169921875,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9U",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 495782278,
      "version": 963,
      "versionNonce": 1942453037,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785750518290,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- A session is the set of interactions between two entities in a given period of time.\n- Spark session provides a unified entrypoint to the spark functionalities  \n- It allows programming using Spark APIs\n- In an interactive spark shell, the spark session is instantiated automatically.\n- In a spark app, the spark session should be created explecitly (from pyspark.sql import sparkSession).\n- There is a one-to-one correspondance between a Spark application and a spark session.\n     - One spark for one application\n- It connects the spark driver with the cluster manager\n- It determines the manager (YARN, Mesos, or Standalone) \n- It allows configurations of spark parameters(optimization and parallelism).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- A session is the set of interactions between two entities in a given period of time.\n- Spark session provides a unified entrypoint to the spark functionalities  \n- It allows programming using Spark APIs\n- In an interactive spark shell, the spark session is instantiated automatically.\n- In a spark app, the spark session should be created explecitly (from pyspark.sql import sparkSession).\n- There is a one-to-one correspondance between a Spark application and a spark session.\n     - One spark for one application\n- It connects the spark driver with the cluster manager\n- It determines the manager (YARN, Mesos, or Standalone) \n- It allows configurations of spark parameters(optimization and parallelism).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
