      "text": "The spark command of to run the spark application: ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The spark command of to run the spark application: ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4EFiy8iPuG5KGwqy6xnel",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 481.2596977402825,
      "y": 6237.176966908314,
      "width": 792,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bAA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 389293590,
      "version": 414,
      "versionNonce": 1090550870,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785242136973,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. The spark submit run on the local machine, making a request to \n    cluster manager driver node to grant resources to the spark \n    driver process only. We assume that the cluster manager accepts the \n    request and place the spark driver process onto a cluster node.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. The spark submit run on the local machine, making a request to \n    cluster manager driver node to grant resources to the spark \n    driver process only. We assume that the cluster manager accepts the \n    request and place the spark driver process onto a cluster node.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
